{"key":"enterprise/T1498.001","id":"T1498.001","name":"Direct Network Flood","domain":"enterprise","level":"subtechnique","parent_id":"T1498","tactics":["impact"],"platforms":["Windows","IaaS","Linux","macOS"],"environments":["cloud","cloud-hosted-endpoint","onprem"],"environment_basis":"project_taxonomy_from_upstream_platforms","summary":"Adversaries may attempt to cause a denial of service (DoS) by directly sending a high-volume of network traffic to a target. This DoS attack may also reduce the availability and functionality of the targeted system(s) and network. Direct Network Floods are when one or more systems are used to send a high-volume of network packets towards the targeted service's network. Almost any network protocol may be used for flooding. Stateless protocols…","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1498/001","source_stix_id":"attack-pattern--0bda01d5-4c1d-4062-8ee2-6872334383c3","source_modified":"2025-10-24T17:48:22.567Z","source_object_version":"1.4","telemetry":{"status":"mapped","components":[{"id":"DC0018","name":"Host Status","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0018","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--85a533a4-5fa4-4dba-b45d-f0717bedd6e6","page":"telemetry/DC0018/"},{"id":"DC0082","name":"Network Connection Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0082","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--181a9f8c-c780-4f1f-91a8-edb770e904ba","page":"telemetry/DC0082/"},{"id":"DC0078","name":"Network Traffic Flow","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0078","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--a7f22107-02e5-4982-9067-6625d4a1765a","page":"telemetry/DC0078/"},{"id":"DC0032","name":"Process Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0032","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3d20385b-24ef-40e1-9f56-f39750379077","page":"telemetry/DC0032/"}],"strategies":[{"id":"DET0343","name":"Direct Network Flood Detection across IaaS, Linux, Windows, and macOS","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategi